atements of financial position\" (T:A:638), not the summary in Item 5. So I'll use T:A:638.\n\nThe value in the summary table (millions): 7,193.1. The value in the primary statement (thousands): 7,193,091. Both are consistent. The primary statement is the correct source.\n\nEvidence quote: I should quote the row with context. Something like:\n\n\"Consolidated statements of financial position — As of December 31, 2025 ... (In thousands of US dollars) ... Total assets ... $ 7,193,091\"\n\nMax 400 chars. Let me construct:\n\n\"Consolidated statements of financial position (As of December 31, 2025, 2024 and 2023; In thousands of US dollars): Total assets | $ 7,193,091 [2025] | 6,383,565 [2024] | 6,091,762 [2023]\"\n\nThat's fine, under 400 chars.\n\nAlso need checked locations? No — for \"found\", the schema requires only \"location\" (single). For not_found/ambiguous, checked_locations are needed. For found, one location object.\n\nLet me also double check the scale: \"Record the statement's scale separately; do not multiply it.\" The statement is \"(In thousands of US dollars)\" so scale = 1000. Value = 7193091.\n\nLet me also confirm there's no ambiguity issue: The document has both a summary table (Item 5, in millions) and the primary statement (in thousands). Both report Total assets for 2025-12-31: 7,193.1 million vs 7,193,091 thousand — consistent. Since the definition requires the consolidated primary balance sheet, the primary statement value is the right one. No ambiguity.\n\nOne more check: the value cell — column \"2025\". The header row: `<S:A:C638.2.6>2025`. Row label \"Total assets\". Good.\n\nPeriod: instant at 2025-12-31. The XBRL context is PAsOn12_31_2025 which confirms instant.\n\nFinal JSON:\n\n{\n  \"schema\": \"statement_candidate_v1\",\n  \"request_id\": \"pilot-aero-summary-neighbour-v1\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"requested_field\": \"Assets\",\n      \"outcome\": \"found\",\n      \"value\": \"7193091\",\n      \"scale\": \"1000\",\n  